          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Is TENCEL more sustainable than cotton?",
            "answer": "<p>TENCEL is made in a closed-loop process that recycles roughly 99% of the solvents used. The wood pulp comes from sustainably managed forests. It uses significantly less water than conventional cotton and avoids pesticide use.</p>"
